		{
			dependencies: ["172EE8617C59F90A"]
			description: [
				"Deep within the &8Forlorn Hollows&r, the &8Underzealots&r perform a sinister ritual in service of an ancient power."
				""
				"Rather than simply hunting their prey, these fanatical cultists seek out peaceful &5Gloomoths&r, offering them as sacrifices to summon a mysterious guardian known only as the &7Watcher&r. Few adventurers have ever witnessed the ceremony firsthand, and even fewer have survived the creature that emerges."
				""
				"Will you uncover the truth behind the ritual, or become another victim claimed by the darkness?"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"To witness the ritual, you must first locate both an &8Underzealot&r and a nearby &5Gloomoth&r."
				""
				"Gloomoths are naturally attracted to &elight sources&r, often circling torches, lanterns, and other glowing blocks. Placing additional light sources near an Underzealot can encourage nearby Gloomoths to approach, increasing the chances of the ritual taking place."
				""
				"Remain nearby and be patient. Once the Underzealot captures a Gloomoth, the sacrifice will begin, transforming the unfortunate creature into a &7Watcher&r."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"The &7Watcher&r is one of the most dangerous creatures found within the Forlorn Hollows."
				""
				"Its powerful attacks and dark magic make it a formidable opponent, rewarding only those capable of overcoming the ritual's final guardian. Defeating the Watcher is the only way to obtain the rare &5Occult Gem&r, a mysterious relic infused with the corrupt energy of the Hollows and required for several advanced crafting recipes later in your adventure."
				""
				"The darkness always demands a sacrifice."
				""
				"Make sure it isn't you."
			]
			id: "5271C7F38BCADF3F"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "64392B80DACB74EE"
					item: {
						Count: 1
						id: "alexscaves:totem_of_possession"
						tag: {
							Damage: 0
						}
					}
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "78672B181CC2098A"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 500
				}
			]
			shape: "pentagon"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "alexscaves:watcher"
				icon: "alexscaves:occult_gem"
				id: "37891D8EF5B00CC2"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			title: "Slay the Watcher"
			x: 17.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["172EE8617C59F90A"]
			description: [
				"The &8Forlorn Hollows&r are home to countless forgotten rituals, but none are more disturbing than those performed by the fanatical &5Underzealots&r."
				""
				"These devoted followers wander the darkness in search of &cVespers&r, strange bat-like creatures that become unwilling participants in an ancient sacrificial ceremony. Once the ritual begins, there is little hope for the unfortunate creature as dark energy slowly transforms it into the monstrous &4Forsaken&r."
				""
				"Witnessing this forbidden ritual is a chilling reminder of the Hollows' corrupted past."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"If you wish to confront the &4Forsaken&r, you'll first need to locate an &5Underzealot&r and a nearby &cVesper&r."
				""
				"The transformation does not happen immediately, so remain nearby and be patient. Given enough time, the Underzealot will begin its ritual, surrounding the Vesper with dark magic until the creature is consumed by the corruption and reborn as the Forsaken."
				""
				"Once the ritual has begun, prepare yourself for battle."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"The &4Forsaken&r is a far more formidable foe than the creatures from which it is born."
				""
				"Its powerful attacks and overwhelming strength make it one of the deadliest inhabitants of the &8Forlorn Hollows&r, rewarding only those capable of surviving the encounter. Defeating the Forsaken grants valuable materials used throughout advanced crafting and later stages of progression, bringing you one step closer to completing the &cTier 6 Rocket&r."
				""
				"In the Hollows, even the innocent are not spared from corruption."
				""
				"Bring an end to the ritual—and the creature it creates."
			]
			icon: "alexscaves:pure_darkness"
