		{
			dependencies: ["1A2C4E8DD4FA3A3A"]
			description: [
				"Radiation has transformed every living creature that calls the &2Toxic Caves&r home."
				""
				"Some have adapted to thrive within the poisoned landscape, while others have evolved into dangerous mutations capable of overwhelming even experienced explorers. Understanding these creatures is just as important as surviving the hostile environment they inhabit."
				""
				"Every encounter teaches another lesson about life within the wasteland."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"The passive &bRadgill&r swims through the polluted waters of the Toxic Caves and serves as an important food source for the mysterious &6Raycat&r."
				""
				"Although Raycats appear intimidating with their glowing skeletal bodies, they are peaceful creatures that can be tamed by feeding them Radgills. Once befriended, a Raycat becomes an invaluable companion, keeping &aNucleepers&r at a safe distance while occasionally curing your &2Irradiated&r status effect."
				""
				"Even in the harshest environments, unlikely allies can still be found."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"Not every inhabitant of the Toxic Caves is so welcoming."
				""
				"Swarms of &2Gammaroaches&r thrive among the radioactive terrain, leaving behind useful &aToxic Paste&r used in numerous crafting recipes. Meanwhile, the devastating &aNucleeper&r stalks the wasteland, slowly charging a catastrophic nuclear explosion capable of devastating anything nearby if not stopped in time."
				""
				"Defeating these creatures rewards valuable materials while preparing you for the far greater dangers that await deeper within the Toxic Caves."
				""
				"Life always finds a way..."
				""
				"Even in the most toxic places imaginable."
			]
