		{
			dependencies: ["1A2C4E8DD4FA3A3A"]
			description: [
				"Your journey through the &2Primordial Caves&r has finally led to this moment."
				""
				"The legendary &dTremorzilla Egg&r you recovered is unlike any other egg you've encountered. It cannot hatch naturally—instead, it requires an immense burst of radiation to awaken the ancient creature sealed within."
				""
				"Fortunately, the &2Toxic Caves&r provide exactly what is needed. Exposing the egg to the explosion of a &aNucleeper&r, a &2Nuclear Furnace&r, or even a &4Nuclear Bomb&r will provide enough radioactive energy to bring the sleeping titan to life."
				""
				"A legend millions of years in the making is about to awaken."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"Once hatched, your newborn &dTremorzilla&r will rapidly grow into one of the largest creatures you'll encounter throughout your adventure."
				""
				"Unlike its prehistoric relatives, Tremorzilla cannot be tamed with food alone. Instead, it must be fed &2Waste Drums&r recovered from the Toxic Caves. It will consume a minimum of four Waste Drums before it begins to trust you, with each additional drum increasing the chance that the creature finally accepts you as its owner."
				""
				"Persistence—and a healthy supply of radioactive waste—will eventually earn its loyalty."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"Once tamed, Tremorzilla becomes one of the most powerful companions in the entire pack."
				""
				"You can command it to &oFollow&r, &oStay&r, or &oWander&r, ride it across the landscape, and unleash its devastating radioactive energy beam once it has fully charged. Its immense strength makes it invaluable for exploration, combat, and overcoming many of the greatest challenges still awaiting you."
				""
				"The greatest beasts are not always your enemies."
